  "result": "Perfect! All payment terms tests pass. Here's the summary:\n\n## Payment Terms Implementation Complete\n\n**\u2705 19 new tests passing** (163 total pass, 8 pre-existing render failures)\n\n### Changes:\n1. **src/errors.js** \u2014 added TERMS_INVALID error code\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** updated:\n   - `createInvoice` now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n   - Validates terms must be one of: 'NET14', 'NET30', 'EOM'\n   - Calculates `dueDate` based on terms:\n     - **NET14**: 14 days after issueDate\n     - **NET30**: 30 days after issueDate  \n     - **EOM**: Last day of the same month as issueDate\n   - Sets both `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` in returned object\n\n3. **test/terms.test.js** \u2014 19 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Default NET30 behavior\n   - All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n   - Invalid/unsupported terms rejection\n   - Cross-month boundaries (NET14, NET30)\n   - Cross-year boundaries (all terms)\n   - Leap year handling (EOM Feb 29)\n   - Different month lengths (28, 29, 30, 31 days)\n   - Property preservation\n\n### Key behaviors:\n- EOM correctly handles February in leap years (2024 \u2192 Feb 29) and non-leap years (2025 \u2192 Feb 28)\n- Due dates properly span month/year boundaries\n- Immutable invoice objects with terms and dueDate included\n- Works seamlessly with existing discount and VAT calculations\n\nTest totals: **171 tests, 163 passing** (8 pre-existing render failures awaiting VAT output format fixes)",
